// §14 entry 22 -- `u4:maior` (explicit byte order on a SUB-byte field) ->
// EXS-E0201 ("unexpected token").
//
// §5.2 "Bit-width fields", rule 3: "Byte order is required above 8 bits
// and is not part of the grammar AT OR BELOW IT. An unannotated multi-byte
// field in a `@transitus` type IS `:nativus` and is therefore already
// EXS-E0321; `u4:maior` does not parse, so it is EXS-E0201. Neither needs a
// new code."
//
// NOT REACHABLE THIS WAVE -- FOUND BY RUNNING, CONTRARY TO THE INITIAL
// PLAN. This entry was scoped as one of the six "lexical, reachable this
// wave" entries, alongside 3/5/18/19/20. It is not, and the other five are:
// checked directly against BOTH this suite's own probe and the real
// `exsc aedifica --diagnostica json`, `u4:maior` produces ZERO diagnostics
// and exit 0 -- the same silent accept as an ordinary, fully valid file.
// The reason is exactly what §5.2 rule 3 already says in different words:
// "does not parse" is a GRAMMAR fact, and grammar is Stage 2 (there is no
// parser: compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both empty, and `exsc` says of
// itself "only aedifica does anything today: it reads a source file,
// applies spec 8.1 and lexes it"). Lexically, `u4` is simply XID_Start
// 'u' + XID_Continue '4' -- ONE ordinary identifier token, not a
// recognized "sub-byte type" shape -- and `maior` is not a reserved word
// either (compiler/x86_64/lexer/keywords.inc's generated 30-word table has
// no entry for it: `:maior`/`:nativus` are grammar sitting after a type,
// never lexicon). So `u4:maior` tokenizes as IDENT(u4) PUNCT(:)
// IDENT(maior) and stops there, cleanly, with nothing left to object to
// until something knows `u4` names a sub-byte width and THEN sees `:maior`
// attached to it.
//
// Recorded as a finding for this suite's report, not silently reclassified
// without saying so (CLAUDE.md's evidence discipline: "never present a
// re-derivation as a restoration" -- and, by the same logic, never let a
// planning assumption stand once running the thing has actually falsified
// it).

@transitus
publica structura Malum2 {
    campus: u4:maior
}

